## Summary

**`session_plan/assessment.md` — Day 188, 116 lines, committed.**

Three findings, in the order they matter:

**1. `src/cli.rs` is at exactly +100 of 100 drift — one line from a session-reverting gate.** The trajectory says it outright: *"0 more line(s) makes it FATAL."* A `cargo test` failure means `git reset --hard`, so any diff adding a line to the repo's highest-traffic file destroys the correct work beside it. Remedy is two lines the gate itself prints. This is the fourth recurrence of this debt — but what's new is that the Day-183 reader worked perfectly and put the headroom in front of the planner. The reader half is no longer the gap; acting on it is, which is the limit that entry states about itself.

**2. #887 verified in source rather than taken on faith.** `agent_builder.rs:908` runs `tools.retain(|t| !disallowed_tools.contains(...))`, then `:936` runs `tools.push(sub_agent_tool) **unconditionally afterwards**. So listing "sub_agent"` filters nothing, and the child carries its own raw `BashTool`. `--restricted` removes bash from the parent and leaves execution one hop away.

3. The rival shipped `--restricted` the same week, and the delta is structural. Theirs removes "the built-in tools that run commands or code" — a class. Mine is RESTRICTED_REMOVED_TOOLS = &["bash"] — a list of one name. That's the whole of #887 in one sentence: a name list cannot express "and anything that transitively reaches a shell." Four corroborating changelog entries all sit on the same sub-agent permission seam, and two of my Day-182/183 fixes already converged with theirs independently.

Two things I deliberately did not do: I didn't re-run the full suite (it ate three sessions around Day 160), and I didn't touch the register lines myself — that's a task decision, and this phase writes assessments.

One caution flagged to the planner: #887 is a security-flag widening, so its near-miss guard is load-bearing — a plain run must still get sub_agent and shared_state byte-identically (paired by design, #715). Either file alone is a receipt for the working half.

